[{"slug": "south-dakota-property-tax-guide", "title": "South Dakota Property Tax Guide: Appeals, Exemptions and Selling With Tax Due", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>South Dakota Property Tax Guide: Appeals, Exemptions and Selling With Tax Due</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in South Dakota</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>South Dakota Property Tax Guide: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a South Dakota Property Tax Guide sale</li><li>Turn the South Dakota Property Tax Guide offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a South Dakota House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>South Dakota property tax is assessed and collected at the local level, and owners can appeal an assessment.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Appeal to the local board of equalization is perfected by mailing or filing a notice of appeal with the clerk of the local board; a mailed appeal&#x27;s postmark is conclusive on timeliness. (SDCL 10-11-16; <a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/api/Statutes/10-11-16.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>The clerk of the local board must be notified of the appeal no later than the Thursday preceding the third Monday in March. (SDCL 10-11-16; <a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/api/Statutes/10-11-16.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>An appeal from the local board to the county board of equalization must be mailed or filed with the county auditor on or before the first Tuesday in April. (SDCL 10-11-23; <a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/10-11-23' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>The director of equalization must assess each tract of real property at its fair market value, using the cost, market and income approaches. (SDCL 10-6-119; <a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/api/Statutes/10-6-119.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Former SDCL 10-6-33 (valuation basis) was transferred to SDCL 10-6-119. (SDCL 10-6-33; <a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/api/Statutes/10-6-33.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>South Dakota sells tax certificates; a tax deed proceeding may begin three years after the certificate sale and within six years. (SDCL 10-25-1; <a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/api/Statutes/10-25-1.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Any person may redeem a tax certificate before a tax deed issues by paying the certificate sum, interest and subsequent taxes. (SDCL 10-24-1; <a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/api/Statutes/10-24-1.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in South Dakota?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy South Dakota houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/south-dakota-probate-process/'>South Dakota Probate Process Explained</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-south-dakota/'>We buy houses in South Dakota</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://dor.sd.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>South Dakota Department of Revenue</a></li><li><a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>South Dakota Codified Laws</a></li><li><a href='https://ujs.sd.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>South Dakota Unified Judicial System</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for South Dakota Property Tax Guide, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"South Dakota\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-south-dakota/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"South Dakota Property Tax Guide: Appeals\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/south-dakota-property-tax-guide/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "South Dakota Property Tax Guide: Appeals", "rank_math_description": "South Dakota property tax: appeals, exemptions, delinquent tax and selling a house with tax due. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "south dakota property tax"}, {"slug": "south-dakota-probate-process", "title": "South Dakota Probate Process and Selling Inherited Property", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>South Dakota Probate Process and Selling Inherited Property</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in South Dakota</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>South Dakota Probate Process and Selling Inherited Property: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a South Dakota Probate Process and Selling Inherited Property sale</li><li>Turn the South Dakota Probate Process and Selling Inherited Property offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a South Dakota House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>South Dakota probate runs through the courts named in the sources below.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Personal property may be collected by affidavit 30 days after death if the entire estate, less liens, does not exceed $100,000, and no personal representative application is pending. (SDCL 29A-3-1201; <a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/api/Statutes/29A-3-1201.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Successors may file an affidavit for real property 60 days after death if the decedent&#x27;s real property interest in the state is $50,000 or less. (SDCL 29A-3-1203; <a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/29A-3-1203' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Real property affidavit must be filed with the register of deeds with a certified death certificate in each county where land is located. (SDCL 29A-3-1203; <a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/29A-3-1203' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Both affidavits require that the decedent owed no Department of Social Services medical assistance debt for nursing home or institutional care. (SDCL 29A-3-1201, 29A-3-1203; <a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/29A-3-1203' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A purchaser or lender in good faith for value takes title free of estate claims when buying from a successor under a real property affidavit. (SDCL 29A-3-1203; <a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/29A-3-1203' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in South Dakota?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy South Dakota houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/south-dakota-property-tax-guide/'>South Dakota Property Tax Guide: Appeals</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-south-dakota/'>We buy houses in South Dakota</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://dor.sd.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>South Dakota Department of Revenue</a></li><li><a href='https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>South Dakota Codified Laws</a></li><li><a href='https://ujs.sd.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>South Dakota Unified Judicial System</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for South Dakota Probate Process and Selling Inherited Property, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"South Dakota\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-south-dakota/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"South Dakota Probate Process Explained\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/south-dakota-probate-process/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "South Dakota Probate Process Explained", "rank_math_description": "South Dakota probate: the court process, small estates and selling an inherited house. Official sources only.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "south dakota probate"}]